  "reason": "The existing evidence is sparse, so the first experiment should test a balanced configuration that explores key design choices (multimodal, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) while keeping costs manageable. Config_004 uses scvi_n200 (moderate RNA encoder) and resnet50 (standard image encoder) with transformer aggregation (powerful but not excessively costly) and weighted fusion, which is a logical starting point to assess the impact of these components on validation accuracy. The expected cost is moderate compared to more complex models like those using imagenet_vit_l or scgpt."  
